32. Data Retention Policies

One area many systems ignore.

Every school should define:

* How long to keep attendance.
* How long to keep login logs.
* When to archive old sessions.
* When to delete temporary files.
* When to remove exported reports.
* Whether graduated students remain active or archived.
* Whether staff records are anonymized after departure.

This should be configurable because different schools and countries have different legal and operational requirements.

⸻

33. Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery

This is often overlooked in products at launch but becomes critical as customers grow.

SKULOS should include:

* Automatic scheduled backups.
* One-click restore (Platform Super Administrator).
* School-level restore options where feasible.
* Backup verification.
* Disaster recovery procedures.
* Maintenance mode with branded messages.
* Data export for schools that leave the platform.

A school should always feel confident that its data is protected.

⸻

34. Billing & License Management

Since SKULOS is a SaaS platform, it needs an internal commercial engine, not just school features.

The Platform Super Administrator should be able to manage:

* Subscription plans.
* Module licensing.
* Student limits.
* Storage limits.
* Trial periods.
* Renewal reminders.
* Upgrade and downgrade workflows.
* Promotional codes.
* Partner discounts.
* Referral rewards.
* Commission tracking for resellers.

