The One Thing I Believe You’re Still Missing

This is the biggest recommendation I can make.

Don’t think of SKULOS as software.

Think of it as a platform with an ecosystem.

In five years, someone shouldn’t say:

“We use SKULOS.”

They should say:

* We use SKULOS Schools for administration.
* We use SKULOS Learn for teaching.
* We use SKULOS Assess for CBT.
* We use SKULOS Sites for our website.
* We use SKULOS AI for lesson planning and academic insights.
* We use SKULOS Connect for parent communication.
* We use SKULOS Analytics for executive reporting.
* We use the SKULOS Marketplace for additional modules.

That shift in thinking changes every architectural decision. You’re no longer building a school management system. You’re building an education technology platform where the School ERP is simply the first and foundational product. I would make this ecosystem vision a dedicated chapter in the documentation because it will influence your branding, pricing, APIs, plugin architecture, mobile strategy, and long-term product roadmap.